From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0058] media: sophgo: SG2002 CSI: complete lane permutation

The four-lane PHY data selector is a permutation, not merely a list of
the active lanes.  The vendor CIF driver fills every logical data slot,
including the unused slots of a two-lane sensor, with the remaining
physical lanes.  The RAW-source adaptation stopped after the active
lanes and consequently programmed duplicate physical lane zero entries.

Track the clock and active data lanes, then populate the unused logical
data slots from the remaining physical lanes.  The LicheeRV Nano beta
mapping (clock 4, data 3/2) now produces 0x1023, matching the vendor
sequence, instead of 0x0023.
---
 drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c b/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c
index 1e6e05f..1ef6a11 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-capture.c
@@ -481,13 +481,29 @@ static void sg2002_configure_lanes(struct sg2002_capture *cap)
 	const struct v4l2_mbus_config_mipi_csi2 *bus = &cap->bus;
 	u32 data_sel = 0;
 	u32 swaps = 0;
+	bool used[SG2002_NUM_PHYS_LANES] = {};
 	u32 route;
 	unsigned int i;
+	unsigned int logical_lane;
 
+	used[bus->clock_lane] = true;
 	for (i = 0; i < bus->num_data_lanes; i++) {
 		data_sel |= (u32)bus->data_lanes[i] << (i * 4);
 		if (bus->lane_polarities[i + 1])
 			swaps |= BIT(8 + i);
+		used[bus->data_lanes[i]] = true;
+	}
+
+	/* The selector is a full four-entry permutation.  Match the vendor
+	 * CIF driver by assigning otherwise-unused physical lanes to the
+	 * inactive logical slots instead of leaving duplicate lane zeroes. */
+	logical_lane = bus->num_data_lanes;
+	for (i = 0; i < SG2002_NUM_PHYS_LANES &&
+	     logical_lane < SG2002_NUM_DATA_LANES; i++) {
+		if (used[i])
+			continue;
+		data_sel |= (u32)i << (logical_lane * 4);
+		logical_lane++;
 	}
 
 	writel(data_sel, cap->wrap + WRAP_PHY4_DATA_SEL);
